WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.208
- We're going to meet up with
an old old friend of mine

00:00:03.208 --> 00:00:08.154
who is now a successful
restauranteur here in Los Angeles.

00:00:08.154 --> 00:00:11.985
Kris has alerted us to some
of the hottest pad thai spots

00:00:11.985 --> 00:00:12.890
in the city.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.005
- Pad thai tour.

00:00:14.005 --> 00:00:15.352
- Yeah, we're on the pad thai tour.

00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:19.944
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.668 --> 00:00:27.495
Your food is very different

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:29.260
than like standard American thai food.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.141
So what is it about it that's different?

00:00:31.141 --> 00:00:32.791
What have you done differently?

00:00:32.791 --> 00:00:34.596
- The only goalI really have with the food

00:00:34.596 --> 00:00:36.709
is to make it as delicious as possible.

00:00:36.709 --> 00:00:39.797
90% of the time that amounts to making it

00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:41.562
in the most traditional way.

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:43.721
It's been boiled down to
just like the essence.

00:00:43.721 --> 00:00:44.650
There are certain things

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.136
about the process that I'll do different

00:00:46.136 --> 00:00:48.179
because I think it makes
a better end product.

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:51.569
- Is there a specific order in
which you put spices together

00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:53.754
that can alter the intensity

00:00:53.754 --> 00:00:55.952
as opposed to just having,
like too much of something?

00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:58.999
- I don't usually try to get
too technical with our food

00:00:58.999 --> 00:01:01.624
and what we do, but I
would break down pad thai

00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:03.018
into like four or five things.

00:01:03.018 --> 00:01:07.290
Technique, meaning how you work
the ingredients in the wok.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.126
The seasoning.

00:01:08.126 --> 00:01:11.121
The quality of the noodles,
is it too soft, is it chewy.

00:01:11.121 --> 00:01:13.397
The fourth thing is just
like, how amped it is.

00:01:13.397 --> 00:01:15.951
It's supposed to have this trifecta of

00:01:15.951 --> 00:01:18.946
kind of tart, kind of
salty, kind of sweet,

00:01:18.946 --> 00:01:20.455
but where it's all in balance.

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:21.291
- I'm hungry now.

00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:22.684
I'm straight-up hungry.

00:01:22.684 --> 00:01:23.729
Can we follow you into the kitchen?

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:24.612
- Yeah.

00:01:24.612 --> 00:01:25.424
- Let's do it.

00:01:27.294 --> 00:01:28.652
- We're going to make the most basic,

00:01:28.652 --> 00:01:31.601
kind of elemental, no frills pad thai.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.853
- Guess who gets the basic one ready?

00:01:33.853 --> 00:01:35.107
- Steven.

00:01:35.107 --> 00:01:36.384
- This guy.

00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:37.800
Oh yeah.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.332
- We're going to throw in the noodles

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.003
and then we put in,
this is basically tofu,

00:01:42.003 --> 00:01:43.535
and sweet radish.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:46.275
This is essentially a basic pad thai.

00:01:46.275 --> 00:01:49.758
Now we're going to do one
that's sort of not as basic.

00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:50.813
It's a little more decadent.

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:52.761
- [Colin] What should we call this one?

00:01:52.761 --> 00:01:54.293
- [Freddie] So I've come
up with the Mandy Moore

00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:55.245
for the basic one.

00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:57.916
And I think for this one we
can step it up to Britney.

00:01:57.916 --> 00:01:59.332
- You guys wanna go try these?

00:01:59.332 --> 00:02:00.214
- Yeah!

00:02:00.214 --> 00:02:01.515
Let's try some Mandy.

00:02:01.515 --> 00:02:03.474
- [Colin] If I'm just ordering
pad thai to get a feel

00:02:03.474 --> 00:02:05.773
for the restaurant, this is how I want it.

00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:07.746
- Pad thai has always been like,

00:02:07.746 --> 00:02:09.140
a Chinese restaurant serves it

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.695
because people demand it so much.

00:02:10.695 --> 00:02:11.763
But then I order that,

00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:14.410
and it's super mushy and wet.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.941
- You can't have wet pad
thai, that is not a good look.

00:02:16.941 --> 00:02:19.704
If it's sort of smoky and
the noodles are cooked

00:02:19.704 --> 00:02:21.283
but kind of chewy still,

00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:22.630
then I've done my job.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.907
- Colin, when you eat food,

00:02:23.907 --> 00:02:27.320
it both makes it look appetizing
and very unappetizing.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:28.357
(laughs)

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:29.572
I don't know how you do it.

00:02:29.572 --> 00:02:31.732
- It's like that thing,
dance like no one's watching

00:02:31.732 --> 00:02:33.816
or whatever, it's like eat
like no one's watching.

00:02:34.146 --> 00:02:37.026
So with the Britney, you want
to get some of the eggy part,

00:02:37.026 --> 00:02:38.163
get some shrimp.

00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:40.207
- That Britney though.

00:02:40.207 --> 00:02:41.432
- That's amped up.

00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:43.829
- [Freddie] I like both, but
I think I like the Mandy.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.199
- I'm feeling Steven today.

00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:46.638
- It's kind of Steven today.

00:02:46.638 --> 00:02:47.799
A little basic.

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:50.237
- This is our pork toro kho my yang.

00:02:50.237 --> 00:02:52.606
So that basically means
I've grilled pig neck.

00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:54.579
- Wow, that's tender.

00:02:54.579 --> 00:02:57.574
- I brought out this beer
because the other component

00:02:57.574 --> 00:03:00.291
of this dish is essentially
the drink that goes with it.

00:03:00.291 --> 00:03:01.731
- Cheers!

00:03:03.681 --> 00:03:05.283
- So we're gonna go check out
some other thai restaurants

00:03:05.283 --> 00:03:06.305
that Kris enjoys.

00:03:06.305 --> 00:03:08.093
I think what we should
do at each restaurant

00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:10.577
is get their pad thai and then also get

00:03:10.577 --> 00:03:12.458
like a specialty item off their menu

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.151
that is their like thing that
you think is really awesome

00:03:15.151 --> 00:03:16.126
at that spot.

00:03:16.126 --> 00:03:19.284
- Let's go to Lacha Somtom,
the papaya salad place.

00:03:19.284 --> 00:03:20.561
- So we're headed to Thai Town,

00:03:20.561 --> 00:03:21.988
one of my favorite places in LA.

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:27.059
Kris had just informed me

00:03:27.059 --> 00:03:28.824
that he gets carsick really easily.

00:03:28.824 --> 00:03:30.194
- So this is gonna be fun.

00:03:30.194 --> 00:03:33.050
- We had the Mandy and
the Britney at your spot,

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.256
so we're on the search for the
Lady Gaga at the next spot.

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:38.454
- I'm pretty confident we
can find the Lady Gaga today.

00:03:48.776 --> 00:03:50.308
- Let's dig in, alright.

00:03:50.308 --> 00:03:52.212
- That's pretty good, oh my god.

00:03:52.212 --> 00:03:54.047
- It's so different from your pad thai.

00:03:54.047 --> 00:03:55.486
- Yeah I like Kris' noodle better.

00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:56.732
- [Steven] I can see that.

00:03:56.732 --> 00:03:58.705
The meat is super crispy.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.586
I kind of like that better.

00:04:00.586 --> 00:04:03.140
- Now Chris does this make you
want to call the paparazzi?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.253
Or are you crazy in love?

00:04:05.253 --> 00:04:07.413
- I think we should taste
the other one first.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.713
- And then judge?

00:04:08.713 --> 00:04:10.927
- We've only been here for
like five minutes by the way.

00:04:10.927 --> 00:04:11.856
Look at this.

00:04:11.856 --> 00:04:14.155
We need to emphasize
that over and over again.

00:04:14.155 --> 00:04:16.796
Colin is a monster on a sailboat.

00:04:16.941 --> 00:04:18.997
- [Colin] This is the crab pad thai.

00:04:19.212 --> 00:04:20.419
Oh man that crab omelette.

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:22.648
- Wow, it's like so
many different flavors.

00:04:22.648 --> 00:04:24.389
Coming together.

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:25.782
- I'm in love with the crab.

00:04:25.782 --> 00:04:27.895
- Papaya salad coming up.

00:04:27.895 --> 00:04:28.917
- What?

00:04:28.917 --> 00:04:30.473
That is not what I was expecting.

00:04:30.473 --> 00:04:32.168
I'm going all fingers.

00:04:32.168 --> 00:04:33.491
They're basically french fries.

00:04:33.491 --> 00:04:35.279
- An onion rings vibe,
but it's less heavy.

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:39.316
- This is a version with
marinaded raw blue crab.

00:04:39.316 --> 00:04:42.218
You basically just suck the
meat and the juice out of it.

00:04:42.218 --> 00:04:43.409
- [Freddie] I eat crabs all the time,

00:04:43.409 --> 00:04:44.988
I've never had raw crab.

00:04:44.988 --> 00:04:47.194
It's a totally different experience.

00:04:47.194 --> 00:04:49.353
- Usually if you have
cooked crab you've gotta

00:04:49.353 --> 00:04:50.677
like pick it out and eat it.

00:04:50.677 --> 00:04:52.743
This is just like coming out at me.

00:04:52.743 --> 00:04:54.322
I feel like an animal eating this,

00:04:54.322 --> 00:04:55.669
and it feels so good.

00:04:55.669 --> 00:04:58.896
- [Freddie] The crab
omelette one was Beyonce.

00:04:58.896 --> 00:05:01.358
She is like super iconic

00:05:01.358 --> 00:05:04.005
and it gives me more
like that comfort feeling

00:05:04.005 --> 00:05:05.792
as opposed to like super crazy out there.

00:05:05.792 --> 00:05:08.474
- I think we found our
Gaga and our Beyonce.

00:05:08.758 --> 00:05:11.242
- I'm not asleep yet,
I'm just getting sleepy.

00:05:11.242 --> 00:05:14.488
Oh man, I get caught
sleeping in every video.

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:20.569
- We're here at the last
stop, this is Pailin.

00:05:20.569 --> 00:05:21.683
We're gonna have pad thai

00:05:21.683 --> 00:05:23.100
and we're gonna have khao soi,

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.725
which is curried noodles.

00:05:24.725 --> 00:05:26.884
- Oh yeah, this looks promising.

00:05:26.884 --> 00:05:28.301
Who is it, Freddie?

00:05:28.301 --> 00:05:30.483
- I wanna say, Ciara.

00:05:30.483 --> 00:05:31.737
It's got the moves.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.807
- It's a Mariah to me, it's full of flair

00:05:35.807 --> 00:05:38.222
but like also knows
the basics really well.

00:05:38.222 --> 00:05:39.685
- I didn't know that pad thai

00:05:39.685 --> 00:05:41.380
could have so many different styles.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.920
- Should we try those noodles?

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.891
I've been eyeing this
guy from the beginning.

00:05:48.361 --> 00:05:49.815
- [Freddie] This is my favorite thing.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:50.929
- [Colin] Yeah this is so good.

00:05:50.929 --> 00:05:51.997
Doesn't this seem like something you'd eat

00:05:51.997 --> 00:05:53.391
on a cold wintry night?

00:05:53.391 --> 00:05:54.528
- Are you eating off your lap?

00:05:54.528 --> 00:05:55.550
- Maybe.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:56.897
- I'm gonna explode right now.

00:05:56.897 --> 00:05:59.845
- Yeah he was saying that we
gotta try the Northern sausage

00:05:59.845 --> 00:06:01.424
and I already ordered it.

00:06:01.424 --> 00:06:04.118
So hopefully it'll come
out in a quick second.

00:06:04.118 --> 00:06:05.488
- Whoa!

00:06:05.488 --> 00:06:07.827
I think my stomach just made room.

00:06:10.015 --> 00:06:11.385
- That's some crazy sausage.

00:06:11.385 --> 00:06:12.778
- That's a great way to
end the day, right here.

00:06:12.778 --> 00:06:14.891
- Thank you Chris, for having us.

00:06:14.891 --> 00:06:16.597
Thai food is more than pad thai.

00:06:16.597 --> 00:06:19.058
I already knew that, but
now that's been reinforced.

00:06:19.058 --> 00:06:20.637
- My mind has been expanded,

00:06:20.637 --> 00:06:24.532
and I know like the
go-tos and what to get.

00:06:24.723 --> 00:06:27.431
- I think I'm realizing now
that I was very ignorant

00:06:27.431 --> 00:06:30.305
with thai food, and like
anything thai related.

00:06:30.729 --> 00:06:32.865
I just got taken to school by Kris today.

00:06:32.865 --> 00:06:33.997
Peace.

